---
import ContentPage from "@/layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import { getMeta } from "@/lib/rm";
const seo = await getMeta("/emergency-service", {
  title: "24/7 Emergency Industrial Repair · Free Nationwide Pickup",
  description: "Equipment down? KMS 24/7 emergency line is answered every day. Free pickup, rush repair, expedited shipping. Call 346-350-1464.",
  ogImage: "/images/kms-hero-bg.webp",
});
---
<ContentPage
  seo={seo}
  h1="24/7 Emergency Industrial Repair"
  subheading="When your equipment is down and every hour costs money, you don't have time to wait. Our emergency line is answered every day of the year — call 346-350-1464."
  bgImage="/images/kms-hero-bg.webp"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Emergency Service" }]}
>
  <div class="content-prose">
    <h2>Call Us — Anytime</h2>
    <p style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700"><a href="tel:3463501464">346-350-1464</a></p>
    <p>Our emergency line is answered 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, every day of the year. No voicemail tree, no callback queue — a real person who can dispatch a response. When your centrifuge crashes at 2 a.m. on a Sunday, that's when you find out what your repair partner is made of.</p>

    <h2>What "Emergency Service" Actually Means</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Immediate response.</strong> We pick up the phone, take the details, and tell you what's possible.</li>
      <li><strong>Free emergency pickup.</strong> We coordinate inbound freight from anywhere in the U.S., Canada, or Mexico, including specialty rigging for oversized equipment.</li>
      <li><strong>Rush intake and processing.</strong> Your unit goes to the front of the queue. We've done 10-day centrifuge rebuilds and 72-hour hydraulic pump repairs when the situation demanded it.</li>
      <li><strong>Expedited return shipping.</strong> Hot-shot, dedicated, or air freight as the situation requires. We don't economy-ship emergency repairs.</li>
      <li><strong>24-month warranty applies.</strong> Emergency repairs get the same written warranty as standard repairs. Speed doesn't compromise quality.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What We Need From You</h2>
    <p>The faster we can get details, the faster we can move. When you call, have ready:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Equipment type, brand, and model (or just a photo of the nameplate — that's enough)</li>
      <li>What failed, or what symptoms you're seeing</li>
      <li>Your location, and how the equipment can be loaded for pickup</li>
      <li>How critical the timeline is — is the plant down, or is there a workaround?</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Don't have everything? Call anyway. We'll figure out what we don't know on the call.</p>

    <h2>What Counts as an Emergency?</h2>
    <p>You decide. If your operation is shut down or about to be, it's an emergency. If you've got a unit in standby and a couple of weeks of runway, it's still a priority job — just not an emergency. We'll be honest with you about which one your situation is and price accordingly.</p>

    <h2>Why Our Customers Trust the Emergency Line</h2>
    <p>Because we answer it. For 40+ years, when industrial customers across the country have called Kelsey Machine at 3 a.m. with a rotating equipment failure, somebody at KMS has picked up the phone. That's not marketing — it's a reputation built one emergency repair at a time.</p>

    <p>Need help right now? <a href="tel:3463501464">Call 346-350-1464</a>. Or if your situation is urgent but not immediate, <a href="/contact">request a quote</a> and tell us your timeline.</p>
  </div>
</ContentPage>
